      "name": {
        "name": "Protein ADMETOS",
        "short": "ADMETOS"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This family consists of plant J domain-containing proteins, including protein ADMETOS from Arabidopsis thaliana. ADMETOS is the product of a dosage-sensitive gene that contributes to the maintenance of paternally and maternally imprinted gene expression in the endosperm, which balances parental contributions [[cite:PUB00167093], [cite:PUB00167094]]. It underlies postzygotic reproductive isolation by promoting triploid seed arrest in a genetic dosage-dependent manner, thus acting as a component of postzygotic interploidy hybridization barriers [[cite:PUB00167094]]. Members of this family typically contain a chaperone J-domain [interpro:IPR036869] and may also feature a zinc \u03b2-ribbon domain.</p>",
          "llm": true,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
